{{#if (eq framework "langgraph")}}
# Debugging the LangGraph project

- The graph is built by `langchain.agents.create_agent` in `agent.py` with two middlewares:
  `ArmatureMiddleware` (reports model calls, runs tools through the runtime) and, when any
  tool needs approval, `HumanInTheLoopMiddleware`.
- `max_steps` is enforced per model call and also sets the graph's recursion limit, with
  headroom. Either way the run ends with `limit_exceeded`; look for repeated tool calls in
  the record.
- An exception inside the model call is reported as `model_error` with the provider's message.
  Check `{{model.api_key_env}}`, the model id and the base URL in `armature.yaml`.
- Approvals pause the graph with an interrupt. The checkpointer
  ({{#if (and session_memory.enabled (eq session_memory.backend "sqlite"))}}`AsyncSqliteSaver` at `ARMATURE_SESSION_DB`{{else}}`InMemorySaver`, lost on restart{{/if}})
  holds the paused state, keyed by the thread id. Resuming sends a `Command` with one decision
  per pending call; a denied call reaches the model as a denial message.
- Conversation state per thread lives in the same checkpointer.
  `GET /threads/{thread_id}` shows what the model will see next turn; `DELETE` clears it.
- To see raw LangChain messages, set a breakpoint in `LangGraphAgent._invoke` and inspect the
  graph result; `to_arc_messages` is the conversion to the run record.
{{/if}}
